from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json,subprocess
p=Path('.tmp/pages-stage-review')
(p/'review.md').write_text('''# Independent Pages raw-tar staging review

Reviewed stage.py, test_stage.py, ci.yml and the final tools/site/README.md section on base b678330 against spec15's same-checked-artifact contract and official upload-pages-artifact action. No implementation edits, actual uploads or Pages mutations.

No blocking finding. Stage validates bounded original raw tar bytes and manifest before xb output; parent-link rejection, existing-file preservation and original-byte return are retained. Canonical serialization is only used internally by recovery validation for comparison, not as replacement output. Existing write failures may leave a partial file but return nonzero; CI does not run the subsequent upload after a failed stage.

Independent 1-test suite passed normally and with python -O. Actual isolated -I CLI execution wrote exactly the known 1177600-byte original tar (SHA-256 cc053272f49f8d4d79fc756560df5401bfdc22b8c1e1a1177ae0250cdc265cd9). Existing output was preserved, wrong digest produced no output, and a real Windows junction output parent was rejected without writing its target. Raw tests and probe outcomes are retained.

Official action source uses the same pinned upload-artifact commit 043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a with a single artifact.tar. CI now stages that same shape from the validated original bytes, then preserves the new upload ID and outer ZIP digest in diagnostic JSON. The names include source/run/attempt. Stage/upload failures fail doc-browser and its required quality gate; the always diagnostic artifact step remains. There are no new Pages/token permissions, and PR uploads are not deployment operations.

Final README correctly distinguishes the outer archive digest from the inner tar digest, partial-output handling, and the remaining authenticated download, CI, freshness, writer-state and publication gates. Action-upload success alone is not current publication, LKG or T16/runtime acceptance. New CI execution and real Pages acceptance of the staged artifact are not independently verified by this local review.

Official source accessed 2026-09-13: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/actions/upload-pages-artifact/main/action.yml (single artifact.tar upload at lines 78-85). The action's own preceding tar generation is intentionally not invoked because the original validated tar already exists.
''',encoding='utf8',newline='\n')
for name in ['tools/site/stage.py','tools/site/test_stage.py','.github/workflows/ci.yml','tools/site/README.md']:
 f=p/'source'/name;f.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);f.write_bytes(Path(name).read_bytes())
(p/'diff.patch').write_bytes(subprocess.run(['git','diff','--','.github/workflows/ci.yml','tools/site/README.md'],capture_output=True,check=True).stdout)
rows=[]
for f in sorted(p.rglob('*')):
 if f.is_file() and f.name!='manifest.json':
  b=f.read_bytes();rows.append(dict(path=f.relative_to(p).as_posix(),bytes=len(b),sha256=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()))
(p/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(files=rows),indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf8');print(len(rows),sum(r['bytes'] for r in rows))
